{title: On my head}
{artist: Dan Bárta}

{start_of_grid shape="3x4" label="I:"}
| D  | F#m | G | % |
| D  | F#m | G | A |
| Bm | %   | % | % |
{end_of_grid}

{start_of_verse: V1:}
[D]Lead my heart in [F#m]my own place
[G]Ride up to the stars across the heaven
[D]Hello, you [F#m]say, you [G]will drive [A]me lazy
Meeting my heart, leaving the yard
Waiting for the night's burst never say never
We freak, we burts, pasting from our angles
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: R1:}
/: [D]When I am standing [F#m]on my head
[G]you are crazy smiling
[D]Now we don’t have it, [F#m]we are mad
[G]go round this speedy [A]romancing :/
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: V1:}
You have the time to take a break
Get up to find your lost control
Someone loves you trust, your soul
Looking for the right size and a good measure
I am a tough guy from the sky
My good will drives me crazy
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: R2:}
/: When I am standing on my head
you are crazy smiling
Now we don’t have it, we are mad
go round this speedy romancing :/ :/
{end_of_chorus}
